{
  "id": "ep009",
  "duration": 47.151,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.466,
      "text": "This smiling salamander can regrow its brain, yet it is nearly gone.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Axolotl-2193331 1280.webp",
        "credit": "LaDameBucolique",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Axolotl-2193331_1280.webp"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.466,
      "end": 11.086,
      "text": "Known as the axolotl, this aquatic amphibian keeps its external gills and never leaves the water.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Dirty-Lucy.webp",
        "credit": "Axolotover",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dirty-Lucy.webp"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.467,
          "end": 11.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.086,
      "end": 17.356,
      "text": "Beyond staying young forever, it can completely regenerate severed limbs, tails, and heart tissue.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Descriptiones et icones amphibiorum (19891378912).jpg",
        "credit": "Wagler, Johann",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Descriptiones_et_icones_amphibiorum_(19891378912).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.1,
          "end": 17.367,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.356,
      "end": 23.626,
      "text": "Nearly all laboratory pets trace back to a single 1864 shipment sent to Paris.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.367,
          "end": 23.633,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.626,
      "end": 29.471,
      "text": "Yet in the shrinking water channels of Lake [Xochimilco](/z\u02c8Ok\u02c8Im\u02c8\u026alk\u02c8O/), the wild population has crashed.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "June 2007 Tourism boating in Xochimilco 28.jpg",
        "credit": "Syced",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:June_2007_Tourism_boating_in_Xochimilco_28.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.633,
          "end": 27.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 27.567,
          "end": 29.467,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 29.471,
      "end": 36.216,
      "text": "Invasive fish like tilapia were introduced and eat their eggs, adding to pollution and urban pressure.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Tilapia fish at Siantar Zoo.jpg",
        "credit": "Nafisathallah",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tilapia_fish_at_Siantar_Zoo.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 29.467,
          "end": 32.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 32.467,
          "end": 36.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.216,
      "end": 43.241,
      "text": "Current surveys show that only about 50 to 1,000 adult axolotls survive in the wild.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "\u767d\u5316\u516d\u89d2\u6050\u9f8d Ambystoma nexicanum albino - panoramio.jpg",
        "credit": "lienyuan lee",
        "license": "CC BY 3.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%99%BD%E5%8C%96%E5%85%AD%E8%A7%92%E6%81%90%E9%BE%8D_Ambystoma_nexicanum_albino_-_panoramio.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.2,
          "end": 39.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 39.0,
          "end": 43.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.241,
      "end": 46.801,
      "text": "This smiling salamander faces a fight to stay on Earth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Axolotl-2193331 1280.webp",
        "credit": "LaDameBucolique",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Axolotl-2193331_1280.webp"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 43.233,
          "end": 47.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
